usage() {
    cat << EOF
Usage: $SCRIPT_NAME [install rke2|ap-bundle|ddpc-bundle|harbor|swfs|velero|monitoring] [uninstall rke2|ap-bundle|ddpc-bundle|harbor|swfs|velero|monitoring [--purge-cache]] [upgrade rke2 [server|agent|both] [stable|<version>]] [offline-prep] [push] [join server|agent [server-fqdn] [join-token-string]] [config hostname|static-ip ...] [-tls-san [server-fqdn-ip]] [-registry [registry:port username password]]

Commands:
  install      : Installs specified component and any dependencies.
                 For air-gapped install, ap-offline.tar.gz file must be in the same directory as script.
    [rke2]       Installs rke2 as a server.
    [ap-bundle]  Extracts the Dell Automation Platform install bundle and outputs the install command.
                 Must be used with [-registry].
    [ddpc-bundle] Stages the Dell Distributed Private Cloud (DDPC) add-on bundle on top of an EXISTING
                 DAP install: pre-checks the cluster, the deployed DAP version, the registry and the
                 resource headroom, then extracts the bundle and outputs the install command.
                 [-registry] is optional: given, the DDPC images are pushed with those credentials;
                 omitted, the orchestrator's existing docker-secret registry is reused.
    [harbor]     Installs the harbor registry.
    [swfs]       Installs a single-node SeaweedFS server for artifact storage.
    [velero]     Installs Velero backup with CSI snapshot support, Longhorn integration, and SeaweedFS S3 storage.
                 Delegates to rke2_installer.sh. Requires VELERO_S3_ACCESS_KEY, VELERO_S3_SECRET_KEY, and VELERO_S3_URL.
    [monitoring] Installs kube-prometheus-stack + Fluent Bit in the RKE2 cluster and configures ServiceMonitor auto-discovery.

  uninstall    : Uninstalls the specified component, reverting only what ap-tools/its sub-installers changed
                 (recorded in /var/lib/ap-tools/state.env and the sub-installers' own state files).
                 Destructive targets (rke2, harbor, swfs) require typing 'yes-destroy' to confirm;
                 set AP_ASSUME_YES=true to skip the prompt in automation.
    [rke2]       Tears down this cluster node via rke2_installer.sh uninstall. DESTROYS Longhorn PVs.
    [ap-bundle]  Removes the DAP staging: bundle tree, ap-install-upgrade-cmd.txt, registry CA trust and
                 docker certs.d entry. Does NOT uninstall DAP itself (DAP lives in the cluster - remove it
                 with 'uninstall rke2' or Dell's own procedure). Does NOT remove docker.
    [ddpc-bundle] Removes the DDPC staging: ddpc-bundle tree and ddpc-install-upgrade-cmd.txt, plus the
                 registry CA trust/certs.d entry ONLY if 'install ddpc-bundle -registry' targeted a registry
                 other than DAP's own. Does NOT uninstall DDPC itself - it prints the helm/kubectl commands that do.
    [harbor]     Delegates to install_harbor.sh uninstall-harbor.
    [swfs]       Delegates to install-seaweedfs uninstall.
    [velero]     Removes Velero from the cluster (S3 backups are kept).
    [monitoring] Removes kube-prometheus-stack + Fluent Bit from the cluster.
    [--purge-cache]  Also remove the ~20GB working cache (\$PWD/ap-install: bundle zip, cached
                 sub-installers, helm charts). Valid with any uninstall target.

  offline-prep : Creates an offline tar package which contains all dependencies for an air-gapped installation.
                 Includes Velero CLI and container images.
                 Cannot be used with [install] [push] [join].

  push         : Pushes all kubernetes and utility container images to the specified registry.
    [-registry]  Must be specified. Does not push Dell Automation Platform images.

  join         : Joins the host to an existing cluster as a [server] or [agent].
    [server] [server-fqdn] [join-token-string]
    [agent]  [server-fqdn] [join-token-string]

  config       : Host preparation helpers. Cannot be combined with other commands.
    [hostname <fqdn>]
                 Sets the hostname (hostnamectl) and reconciles a marker-tagged /etc/hosts entry
                 (127.0.1.1 line on Debian-family; '<MGMT_IP> <fqdn> <short>' on Rocky/Leap).
                 Refuses to run while an RKE2 service is active (hostname = node identity).
    [static-ip -ip <addr>/<prefix> -gw <gateway> -dns <srv1[,srv2]> [-domain <search>] [-interface <if>] [--apply] [--force-ssh-interface]]
                 Default is GENERATE+VALIDATE only: prints the netplan YAML (Ubuntu) or nmcli
                 commands (Rocky/Leap) that would be applied. --apply activates it:
                 Ubuntu uses 'netplan try' (120s auto-rollback); Rocky/Leap apply with a
                 scheduled 120s auto-revert that must be confirmed with 'config static-ip commit'.
                 Refuses the SSH-carrying interface without --force-ssh-interface.
    [static-ip commit]
                 Confirms a pending Rocky/Leap static-ip change (cancels the auto-revert).

  -tls-san     : When provided,adds specified FQDN to rke2 tls-san configuration for multi-node setup.
                 Used with [install rke2] or [join server]. [server-fqdn-ip] must be a valid IP or FQDN.
        [server-fqdn-ip]

  upgrade      : Upgrades RKE2 cluster nodes using system-upgrade-controller.
                 Delegates to rke2_installer.sh. Only supports rke2 at this time.
    [rke2]       Upgrade target. Only 'rke2' is supported.
      [server|agent|both]  Nodes to upgrade: server (control-plane), agent (workers), or both.
      [stable|<version>]   Target version: 'stable' for latest, or specific version (e.g. v1.33.4+rke2r1).

  -registry    : Used with [install rke2], [install ap-bundle], [install ddpc-bundle], [push], and [upgrade rke2] to provide a valid registry and credentials.
    [registry:port username password]

EOF
    exit 1
}

